      "reasoning": "This is an objective criterion. The report accurately reproduces the cumulative loss, both half-period rates, the 36% central acceleration, and the 2023 maximum, but reports a different acceleration uncertainty (±16.8 rather than ±10 percentage points) and entirely omits the required quantitative comparison showing glacier loss was 18% greater than Greenland’s and more than twice Antarctica’s."
     },
     {
      "index": 1,
      "type": "image",
      "weight": 0.1,
      "score": 36,
      "reasoning": "This is an objective quantitative criterion. The contribution plot correctly reproduces the leading absolute contributors—Alaska (~22%), combined Arctic Canada (~20%), Greenland periphery (~13%), and Southern Andes (~10%)—and includes specific mass-change rates, but it omits 2000 ice volumes and therefore does not show or verify the required relative volume-loss rankings and percentages."
     },
     {
      "index": 2,
      "type": "image",
      "weight": 0.2,
      "score": 27,
      "reasoning": "This is Mode A because the criterion requires specific cross-method quantitative comparisons. The report includes matched-period method plots and variability correlations, but compares against a combined DEM+glaciological product rather than DEM differencing alone, omits the required glaciological-site bias analysis, and does not clearly reproduce the stated aggregate differences of 0.08 ± 0.08 and 0.02 ± 0.08 m w.e. yr⁻¹; therefore the visual analysis is only a partial and methodologically mismatched substitute for the target."
     },
